<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">10 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 10 October, from 732 to 1967.</p></header>
<div class="tih-pinned-card"><p class="tih-pinned-label">International day</p><p class="tih-pinned-title">World Mental Health Day</p><p class="tih-pinned-desc">Observed since 1992 under the World Federation for Mental Health and endorsed by the World Health Organisation, World Mental Health Day promotes global awareness of mental health issues and advocates for open discussion and improved access to care.</p></div>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/charles-martel" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-martel.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/732">732 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,294 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles Martel defeats an Umayyad army near Tours</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Frankish forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-martel">Charles Martel</a> defeated an Arab and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> army led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-al-ghafiqi">Abd al-Rahman al-Ghafiqi</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tours">Tours</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poitiers">Poitiers</a>; the traditional date is 10 October. How decisive the battle was remains debated.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-martel">Charles Martel</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1845">1845 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">181 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The US Naval School opens at Annapolis</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Naval School, renamed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Naval Academy in 1850, opened at Fort Severn in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/annapolis-maryland">Annapolis, Maryland</a>, with 50 midshipmen. It has trained American naval officers ever since; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jimmy-carter">Jimmy Carter</a> was among its graduates.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1911">1911 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">115 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Wuchang Uprising sparks the Chinese revolution</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Revolutionary soldiers mutinied at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wuchang">Wuchang</a>, beginning the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinhai-revolution">Xinhai Revolution</a>. Within months the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing dynasty</a> abdicated, ending more than two thousand years of imperial rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinhai-revolution">Xinhai Revolution</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wuchang">Wuchang</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1913">1913 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">113 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Woodrow Wilson triggers the blast that floods the Panama Canal cut</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">From the White House, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/woodrow-wilson">President Wilson</a> sent a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telegraph">telegraph</a> signal that detonated the Gamboa dike. Water flowed into the Culebra Cut, joining the canal's waters ten months before it opened to shipping.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/woodrow-wilson">Woodrow Wilson</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1967">1967 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">59 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Outer Space Treaty enters into force</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Outer Space Treaty came into effect, forming the basis of international space law. It bars nuclear weapons from orbit and forbids any nation from claiming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhu">Moon</a> or other celestial bodies.</p></div></li></ol>
